# the effects' one pool (dsp/efx.h, 78 blocks of 2 KB): a new project's sends (FX I's delay, 24 blocks; FX II's lush,
# 26) leave room for a track's delay (24) beside them; a second track's delay finds none ("no memory": it passes dry).
# (The sends each their own blocks: FX II placed beside FX I, not over it, engine.c pool_sends; over it, the tracks
# had 26 blocks more, and the second delay found room). Master FX after the sends, before the tracks: its delay (24)
# takes a track's room, its tape a block
wait 300
expect fxroom1 1
expect fxroom2 1
expect room1.1 1
knob 1 ctype 16
knob 1 cmix 100
wait 100
expect par1.ctype 16
expect room1.1 1
expect fxroom1 1
expect fxroom2 1
knob 2 ctype 16
knob 2 cmix 100
wait 100
expect room2.1 0
expect room1.1 1
# the first track's delay off: its blocks go to the second's
knob 1 ctype 0
wait 100
expect room2.1 1
expect fxroom1 1
expect fxroom2 1
# Master FX's delay: its memory before the tracks' (the second track's delay gives its blocks up); its tape's wow a
# block, the track's delay back beside it
mst color delay
mst cmix 64
wait 100
expect mstroom 1
expect room2.1 0
expect fxroom1 1
expect fxroom2 1
mst color tape
wait 100
expect mstroom 1
expect room2.1 1
mst color off
wait 100
expect mstroom 1
expect room2.1 1
